## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about memory access patterns and cache locality in a practical loop, not just algorithmic correctness.

## Key Concepts
- Cache locality
- Blocking/tiling
- L1 data reuse
- Edge-case handling

## Code Example
```javascript
void transpose(int N, int M, const int A[][M], int B[][N]) {
  const int BS = 16;
  for (int r = 0; r < N; r += BS)
    for (int c = 0; c < M; c += BS) {
      int rmax = (r + BS > N) ? N : r + BS;
      int cmax = (c + BS > M) ? M : c + BS;
      for (int i = r; i < rmax; ++i)
        for (int j = c; j < cmax; ++j)
          B[j][i] = A[i][j];
    }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you benchmark the cache miss rate vs a naive row-major transpose?
- How does tile size affect performance on different CPU architectures?

